    "updated_at": "2016-06-07T00:19:35Z",
    "body": "@sicking I was hoping for an initial consensus on the existing two-browser behavior, instead of continuing to try to come up with an ideal API which will get stuck for another 4 years :-/. After agreeing on removing `readonly`, we could try pushing for changing the type, but that would require more implementer interest beyond just Mozilla, which I haven't seen in any of the linked threads.\n",
